<title>USA: Airgas sets new shareholder rights plan.</title>
<headline>Airgas sets new shareholder rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>RADNOR, Pa. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airgas Inc said Thursday it would put in place a new defensive stockholder rights plan to replace an existing plan that expires in 1998.</p>
<p>Common stock issued after April 29, 1997, will include an attached right entitling the holder to purchase 0.001 share of preferred stock at an initial exercise price of $100 per share.</p>
<p>Rights become exercisable following the acquisition by a person or group of 15 percent -- or 20 percent in the case of Peter McCausland and his affiliates -- or more of Airgas's stock.</p>
<p>McCausland is chief executive of Airgas.</p>
<p>((--David Chance, New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
